{
  "name": "SettingClassIsAType",
  "comment": "Settings are settings, not kinds (ruling 7, decision 774). Each settings class is a\ntop-level type of its own, named by its namespace: the llm settings class lives at\napp.module.llm.setting, so its type.name is `app.module.llm.setting`. No type is\nrenamed — looking it up by that namespace name answers with that same name. Red today:\ntoday the llm settings class is a kind under a shared `setting` family (decision 48),\nso `%!llm.setting!type.name%` reads `\"setting\"`, not `\"app.module.llm.setting\"`.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "assert.equals(Expected=\"app.module.llm.setting\", Actual=%!llm.setting!type.name%, Message=\"llm settings class is a type named by its namespace\")",
